                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "clad",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                        "entry_id": "0b524a49-bd72-3c4d-ae5f-ed27d2fc4a8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wearing clothing or some other covering (for example, an armour) on the body; clothed, dressed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f2d6ff0-a7ef-47c0-bf64-a51e7a0f8ac5",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "[...] from his nook up leapt the venturous lad, / And flinging wide the cedar-carven door / Beheld an awful image saffron-clad / And armed for battle!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69f928c0-3487-4f1d-9dda-7f4dbd30589a",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "Her downcast eyes were almost mesmerized by the huge tweed-clad knees which towered like monoliths beside her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa08f75a-9333-4e1a-8c22-d8877e032adc",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "Everything was lost in a scene from a movie in which khaki-clad regiments marched fast, fast across the scene."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12f82613-4d1e-4894-9417-0a70620b93d6",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "The radical conservatives of the Jain monks were called “Digambara—the sky-clad.” They went about completely naked, or in other words, “clothed in space.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47a57ce1-e13c-41ce-90bc-3a4608b9b40e",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "There his chains would be removed and he would be ushered into the waiting-room for a five-minute chat with his wife surrounded on all sides by security men and civilian-clad prison warders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d737307-d560-4723-9c3a-74518c0d655f",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "Love brought between my sheets a laughing lad / One night. Eighteen years old, he was half-clad / Like a young boy: what a sweet dream!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b098d4b-6b92-496c-b317-63ae50138775",
                                                "sense_id": "4b2814ca-bd6b-3dcc-a577-c436ea612f53",
                                                "text": "In the original photograph, the two leaders are followed by a single pair of uniform-clad men, but in Kafka's symmetrical arrangement, there are two pairs of attendants, each pair facing each other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                        "entry_id": "0b524a49-bd72-3c4d-ae5f-ed27d2fc4a8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Covered, enveloped in, or surrounded by a cladding, or a specified material or substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-compounds",
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdfda327-27b0-44dd-97db-987893455854",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "On all sides, Goudet is shut in by mountains; rocky foot-paths, practicable at best for donkeys, join it to the outer world of France; and the men and women drink and swear, in their green corner, or look up at the snow-clad peaks in winter from the threshold of their homes [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54d05ff2-fede-48d2-9de9-ede501128802",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "Into this book-clad room it followed the Bishop, with blue eyes and laughter on the red lips [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff7841b8-00d3-4794-9519-84c5c0553ec7",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "The sun has gone down, and the water has gone down / From the weed-clad rock, but the distant cloud-wall rises."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "048d2645-21e0-40a8-a6bf-88d8b2254dca",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "[...] I can remember every volume among the three or four hundred books that made up the library of my father, the country doctor—three or four hundred besides those portentous leather-clad depositories of medical mystery filled with color plates depicting the awful intimacies of the innards;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0042e684-3926-47f1-97ab-82b9dbbaae66",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "Copper and copper-clad steel resist corrosion indefinitely in soil that is relatively free from ammonia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b923e76-8f71-4922-9fd0-78b214582b29",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "The probe is constructed from plastic-clad silica fiber with an FPA Teflon jacket to prevent ambient light from being scattered into the system."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71d588b0-6d9b-4929-bd76-72f860c48597",
                                                "sense_id": "c03cbc8b-5426-37bd-b7b8-c05a07dec80c",
                                                "text": "The second half of the century also saw the artistic peak of ceramic production at İzniq, with the finest products of the İzniq kilns made visible to the public in the tile-clad walls of the mosques of Rüstem Pasha (968/1561) and Șoqollu Meḥmed Pasha (979/1571) in Istanbul, both by Sinān."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7facb8b9-11ad-338f-8d53-49fc3c738489",
                                        "entry_id": "0b524a49-bd72-3c4d-ae5f-ed27d2fc4a8a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Adorned, ornamented."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "clad",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                        "entry_id": "4fa6562e-d3cf-3151-9f61-481ffef95c48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To clothe, to dress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "literary",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2be147ad-e3bb-48b3-b1f7-1d36749f6230",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "At last faire Heſperus in higheſt ſkie / Had ſpent his lãpe [i.e., lampe] and brought forth dawning light, / Then vp he roſe, and clad him haſtily; / The dwarfe him brought his ſteed: ſo both away do fly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bc24ede-18bb-4ebe-a101-db0f26020c4a",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "Muſicke and Poetry is his delight, / Therefore ile haue Italian Maskes by night, / Sweete ſpeeches, Comedies, and pleaſing ſhowes, / And in the day when he ſhall walke abroad, / Like Siluian Nimphs my Pages ſhall be clad, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "384eb9cb-82af-4d80-92c9-1eb056c9390f",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "But ſee the Sunne in ruſſet mantle clad, / Walkes ore the deaw of yon hie mountaine top, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19962b8b-ef7d-464c-8cd7-d9b45ef96e0c",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "And it came to paſſe at that time when Jeroboam went out of Jeruſalem, that the Prophet Ahiiah the Shilonite found him in the way: and hee had clad himſelfe with a new garment; and they two were alone in the field."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bc543a5-cecd-4809-ad39-e67cea5628d9",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "He alwaie claddeth yⁿ a blak Cote with Trunkhose o yᵉ lyke Colore, wi Shoos and Siller Buckels, a spuddish coroned Hatte, wi a Bruarte o muche brodeneſse, an tached vppe atte yᵉ Rear, wi a Cordige an Tassle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cda4d82-57e5-481c-b08a-798c13dfb2c7",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "Those to whom the King had entruſted me, obſerving how ill I was clad, ordered a Taylor to come next Morning, and take my Meaſure for a Suit of Clothes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fa609bb-5994-4c2f-8326-571d0028cb17",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "She had a rustic, woodland air, / And she was wildly clad; / Her eyes were fair, and very fair, / —Her beauty made me glad."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e498c80-4c14-4d7f-abc9-b8f6fc384eca",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "O Pergubri! thou it is that sendest the winter away, and bringest back the beautiful spring. It is thou who coverest the hedges and the meadows with green, and claddest the hedges and the forest with leaves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "534b0cc3-eb99-40fa-b45f-fedfe8fb6ddc",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "Those ladies came over to champion \"Woman's rights,\" and proclaim the equality of the sexes; and to show they had a right to do so, they assumed, or rather usurped male attire—they clad themselves in breeches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b48f6b3b-9506-4576-ad79-8ebc7b671cae",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "But what interested me most was the slender figure of a dainty girl, clad only in a thin bit of muslin which scarce covered her knees—a bit of muslin torn and ragged about the lower hem."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "866129ba-942e-43d5-b975-d1c5311aa0ad",
                                                "sense_id": "c8159043-f13a-3b54-a50d-e2c90d5347de",
                                                "text": "His followers were neither ideologues nor philosophers nor clerics but shabbily clad fifteen-year-olds who looked twice their age and who subsisted on dried corn, fruit, or animal flesh and followed officers with uniforms made out of blankets with cut-out holes for their heads."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                        "entry_id": "4fa6562e-d3cf-3151-9f61-481ffef95c48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cover with a cladding or another material (for example, insulation)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29f7da48-b038-4d70-884c-094f9cc50299",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "[M]any bitter and extreme frosts at midsummer continually clothe and clad the discomfortable mountaines; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4cac5e2-13bc-4767-9886-c74358e72a3e",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "He ſcarce had ſaid, when the bare Earth, till then / Deſert and bare, unſightly, unadorn'd, / Brought forth the tender Graſs whoſe verdure clad / Her Univerſal Face with pleaſant green, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3648237e-5ebe-4c40-bb14-26a4f324e6e7",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "But on the pale moon Eve now fix'd her gaze, / „Behold”, she said, „how cold and pale its face, / „Now Abel’s house it claddeth with its ray, / „And shineth now above Cain’s lonely way.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "246ba210-0363-4869-b9d6-4de5bc0f3c76",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "There, on a rock, he saw a little child. Naked she was, though clad with soft white moonlight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92446b84-705c-42bc-89c3-fad8bb40fcfd",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "Subsequently E. H. Dix, Jr., at Alcoa Research Laboratories established methods to metallurgically clad commercial aluminum to both sides of a 2017-T4 (then known as 17S-T) sheet to obtain outstanding corrosion protection[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6f1cbcf-cfd2-4f01-8d88-5714240c6270",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "[T]he most effective materials at preventing oxygen diffusion are metals or ceramics of a thickness on the order of 1 millimeter or more. This type of coating may not be easily incorporated into the design or easily cladded to the polymer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "beffe1f4-d23e-4088-9e01-082b22a1c2a9",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "The visible surface conveys a building's image. […] It is the thin membrane that clads the walls of both the interior and exterior of the building, and thus constitutes its \"facades.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f5f5edd-08b4-4a3f-b2ca-66b2ff7d933a",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "[A] wrinkled moon strvaigs / across the field of stars, pewters each thistle / spear, and clads each thread of down in light."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "722c5737-b623-48f5-a284-8ec57567acbb",
                                                "sense_id": "39722ef2-1d35-31e8-93f8-92cb78cf3bed",
                                                "text": "The best method, but also the most expensive is cladding the billets in copper. Clad billets can be heated in an induction furnace and lubrication with oil-graphite suffices similar to standard copper alloys."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b33634f-f125-3636-afdf-3bad692b512b",
                                        "entry_id": "4fa6562e-d3cf-3151-9f61-481ffef95c48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To imbue (with a specified quality); to envelop or surround."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cb4e607-ea41-47e2-8e34-4289b458bb15",
                                                "sense_id": "9b33634f-f125-3636-afdf-3bad692b512b",
                                                "text": "Moſt mercifull father, we beſeche thee ſo to ſende vpon theſe thy ſeruauntes thy heauenly bleſſyng, that they maye be cladde about with all iuſtice, & that thy worde ſpoken by theyr mouthes, may haue ſuch ſucceſſe, that it may neuer be ſpoken in vain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f5369ff-efcb-4ff1-baec-e35d6a321142",
                                                "sense_id": "9b33634f-f125-3636-afdf-3bad692b512b",
                                                "text": "O folly, thou hast power to make flesh glad, / When the rich soul in wretchedness is clad."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c51819ae-562d-41a0-8b17-b599d84ed051",
                                                "sense_id": "9b33634f-f125-3636-afdf-3bad692b512b",
                                                "text": "The other day I was looking up some records of the Parliamentary Debates of the past, and I found my hon. Friend the Member for Dundee (Mr. [Dingle] Foot), who is now clad in all the majesty of a Minister and sits on the Treasury bench without regard to his murky past, moved a Motion on one of those pleasant Fridays to which I have referred, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b632c88-d507-4abe-84d0-7ed55c5e690f",
                                                "sense_id": "9b33634f-f125-3636-afdf-3bad692b512b",
                                                "text": "He is one of those bulky men clad in sensitivity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
